\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Motivation and aim}
\date{2026-11-05}


\p{The continuum is widely used to model physical reality. We take it to have
no physical counterpart at quantum-spacetime scales. The measurement limits are
lengths and times below the Planck length and the Planck time
\citet{Section 3.1}{hossenfelder2013minimal}. The notes read the corresponding
energy bound operationally, for physical interactions: concentrating more than
about the Planck energy in a probe's interaction region does not resolve shorter
lengths \citet{Section 3.1.1}{hossenfelder2013minimal}. A minimal length
does not by itself force discreteness
\citet{Section 5}{hossenfelder2013minimal}. Carlip records that the divergences
reflect ignorance of physics at very high energies, that singularities are a
cause for concern, and that no one has proven that quantizing gravity eliminates
them \citet{Section 2}{carlip2001quantum}. Wilson argues that every continuous
model suffers both an ultraviolet catastrophe and an infrared catastrophe
\citet{reply of 12 April 2022, 8:56 am}{wilson2022mathematicism}. Attempts to
quantize gravity have brought the difficulty into focus, since those singularities
and the infinities of perturbation theory are among the problems they hope to
resolve.}

\p{Although we take the continuum as an extrapolation rather than an
observation, lattice field theory keeps the continuum theory as its object and
uses the lattice to compute and to regulate. The spacing is a short-distance
cutoff, removed in the continuum limit as that spacing goes to zero
\citet{Section 7}{wingate2025lattice},
\citet{Section 3.7}{hossenfelder2013minimal}.}

\p{We take the proper mathematical tools for these challenges to be a theory that is
fundamentally discrete, with the finite structure as the object and the
continuum an emergent, large-scale description. The notes therefore build the
mathematics for such a physics from finite structures, by exact algebra and
with no limits inside those finite constructions, and ask whether geometry,
time and matter can be induced from them, revealing new physics insight near
the Planck scale while agreeing with continuum physics at large scales.}

\p{An equally important question concerns the parameters of a model: which
should be determined and which left free, and what principle governs the
division? Cosmological bubble-universe pictures describe regions that may
settle into different vacuum states, with different effective low-energy
physics \citet{§§2–3}{guth2007eternal}. Wilson separately proposes that
particle masses depend on the surrounding gravitational environment
\citek{wilson2020vacua}. We draw inspiration from these pictures and extend
them into a mental model for the mathematics developed here, without adopting
a particular mechanism for forming a bubble.}

\p{In our picture, a bubble universe must have symmetries that allow it to
persist and develop rich physical structure. A particular bubble must “pick”
one such symmetry structure. Ideally, most fundamental parameters would follow
from the chosen symmetries. Among those left free by symmetry, some would be
fixed by the bubble’s initial conditions. Others would depend on the local
background, so describing a concrete physical process would require specifying
its surrounding environment.}

\p{Background independence is usually counted a desirable feature of a fundamental
theory, and Wilson argues that it is a hidden assumption rather than a property the
Standard Model possesses \citek{wilson2025background}. Here the background is the
local environment. Mach's principle says that inertia is determined by the
distribution of matter. The further claim, that fundamental parameters may depend
on that environment, is Wilson's reading of the principle, and the notes keep
their constructions compatible with a physics in which a parameter may so depend.}

\p{Physics motivates the notes, but the interest and the focus are the mathematics
that answers the challenges: no physical theory is claimed, and where the notes
include a falsifiable proposal for one, it is an example of applying the tools
developed here. The organizing
hypothesis is that operations which continuum analysis presents analytically can
be recast as algebra on finite-dimensional objects; the notes test it on small
cases before relying on it, and a proposed translation carries its carrier, its
map and the property proved of it.}
